    rdf:value """Monday, February 5, 1906
Grey and windy.
Worked over Veronese.
Placci came to tea. I called on the Platonoff.
Wrote to Mother, Ray, Ellie, Mr. Putnam, Don Guido,  Mr. Scott, Mr. Keyne s, Britten, Reinach, Cagnola, Logan, Mrs. Remington, Dr. Heath, Mother Superior Mantellati.
Tuesday, February 6, 1906
Very windy, grey, cold.
Worked on Veronese, B.B. on Piedmontese. The parish priest of Badia di Isola (Guido Profeti) came to lunch. We called on Mrs. Ross and the Markbys, on Brauer and then on the Thorolds.
Wrote Rezia Corsini, Maud Cruttwell, Grace, Mrs. Berenson, Christina, Mother.
Wednesday, February 7, 1906
Windy and cold.
Mother’s 74th Birthday.
B.B. went to Academy and Santa Croce with Miss Blood. I typed more Veronese.
In the afternoon we left cards on Mrs. Middlemore and Mme Zoubow and called on the Houghtons who have just got back. He has bought  two  telescopes!
B.B. wrote to Mrs. Gardner and D’Annunzio.
Wrote Holmes (Burlington), Roger (Terburgh), Maud Cruttwell, Guido (twice!), Mother, Mrs. Fletcher Vane."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 46 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1906> .

